# Frontend auth

Shared governor for identity and membership. Executor: `.cursor/skills/frontend/auth/frontend-auth-session/SKILL.md`. Detail SSOT: `frontend/lib/auth/README.md`.

## Hard rules

- `lib/auth/` is client-safe only — no Mongo writes, no firebase-admin.
- Session/membership/policy live in `server/auth/` with `server-only`.
- **Schema SSOT:** `UserDoc` / membership fields and related enums live in `backend/src/db/types.ts` (`.cursor/skills/backend/backend-db/SKILL.md`) — do not invent parallel membership Doc types on the FE.
- Admin mutations: `assertCallerIsAdmin`; target tenant/user/coupon by id or slug (`getTenantObjectIdByName`).
- Non-admin: one tenant membership per Firebase uid; admins may have many.
- Public/middleware actions must not import `@/server/auth` / firebase-admin at top level.
- Do not delete shared `leads` docs on user/tenant cleanup — only user-owned memberships.
- Cookie/session entrypoints (`auth-actions`) are auth-owned — not the generic `mutations.mdc` CRUD envelope.
